cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below, and also cite Justin Alick's original repository (listed under references)."
title: "collatz-m-cycles: no nontrivial positive Collatz cycle has 111 or fewer local minima (Lean 4)"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 kernel-checked proof that every nontrivial positive Collatz cycle has at least 112 local minima
  (no m-cycle with m <= 111), assuming two published inputs stated in the README, plus a computed and
  independently recomputed extension to m <= 127 that is not formally verified. It extends Justin Alick's
  Lean proof for m <= 101 and builds on Hercher (2023). The new work was generated by AI (Claude, Anthropic)
  under Lee Marshall's direction; see the README's disclosure section.
authors:
  - family-names: Marshall
    given-names: Lee
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/LeeMarshall1113/collatz-m-cycles"
keywords: [Collatz conjecture, Lean 4, formal verification, m-cycles]
